            <ArticleTitle>Experiences with electrical stimulation devices for the control of chronic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>217-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The results of a study involving the treatment of pain syndromes by electrical stimulation in 98 patients are reported. Advantages and disadvantages of three electrostimulation techniques--transcutaneous stimulation, peripheral nerve stimulation, and dorsal cord stimulation--are discussed. Also included is a brief discussion of the possible mechanism of suppression of pain stimuli.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
